{{!
    @template local_oksigeniaaty/mobile_work_alert

    A line of «Your work» (local\yourwork): something waiting to be sorted out, with the logo of its service on its light
    plate, what it is and of which service. The whole line opens where it is sorted out; an urgent one has the edge of
    danger and, for screen readers, «Urgent:» before its text. When it is due only orders the list, as in the block: the
    text says the hour that matters.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * text, service, icon, urgent - What it is.
    * unknown - Its service did not answer: a question mark and a broken outline; the text says since when.
    * url, browser - Where it is sorted out, a page of the web: in the app's window, signed in, never through a plugin's
      handler of links (see mobile_work_door); in the phone's browser for the pages a plugin wants there.

    A line without a text is none: the example, empty, draws nothing, because what the app compiles is not HTML that the
    checks of the templates take.

    Example context (json):
    {}
}}
{{#text}}
<a class="aty-event aty-aviso{{#urgent}} aty-urgent{{/urgent}}{{#unknown}} aty-callado{{/unknown}}" core-link href="{{url}}" capture="false"{{^browser}} inApp="true"{{/browser}}>
    <span class="aty-servicio-logo">{{#icon}}<img src="{{icon}}" alt="">{{/icon}}</span>
    <span class="aty-event-body">
        <span class="aty-event-name">{{#urgent}}<span class="sr-only">{{#str}} yourwork:urgent, local_oksigeniaaty {{/str}} </span>{{/urgent}}{{text}}</span>
        {{#service}}<span class="aty-event-context">{{service}}</span>{{/service}}
    </span>
    {{#unknown}}<span class="aty-duda" aria-hidden="true">?</span>{{/unknown}}
</a>
{{/text}}
